            <ArticleTitle>Colonic obstruction caused by intraluminal haematoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2012-006801</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2012006801</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a rare case of caecal obstruction in an anticoagulated elderly patient, who presented with abdominal pain and per-rectal bleeding. CT revealed obstruction in the ascending colon. The patient subsequently underwent a right hemicolectomy for a massively distended caecum containing a large intraluminal haematoma causing obstruction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
